  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A heater of power <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> provides energy to a liquid at its boiling point. A mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> of the liquid vaporizes in time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span>. The specific latent heat of vaporization is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>. How much energy is transferred to the surroundings in time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span>?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Pt+mL\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Pt-mL\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mL}{Pt}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Pt}{mL}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
